gm.\nIntroduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice? It introduces middleware but relationship between R&D and compliance unchanged? It's slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious.\nCommon, mundane? Unified logging substrate is common practice. Score 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably JSON.\n\nProvide lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P2097\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness 4\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure order: effectiveness, applicability, acceptability, implementability, paradigm_relatedness, originality.\n\nReturn rating.\n\n",
