g shows some imagination =3\ninteresting=2\ncommon mundane boring=1\n\nIs shared logging framework embedded in pipeline with DOI? Probably unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. Not necessarily never expressed before. Might be 3. Could be 4? \"may be humorous\". Hmm. Open research observability instrumentation layer... maybe unusual but not ingenious? I think 3.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\n3 = solves implied problem...\nProposal auto-emits Article12 compliant records timestamps reference databases matched inputs verifier identities. That's directly solving logging mandate. So applicability 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\nAuto-emit compliant records... seems would solve logging mandate. Yes 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4): easy to implement low cost or non-radical changes=4\nsome changes reasonably feasible=3\nsignificant change expensive/difficult but not impossible=2\ntotally infeasible=1\n\nShared logging framework embedded in containerised pipeline, extend existing metadata layer with category-aware schema generator... Might be significant change? It says extend existing metadata layer. Some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Requires engineering. Probably 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4): common strategies violate no norms=4\nsomewhat uncommon unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities=3\noffends sensibilities somewhat=2\nradically violates laws...=1\n\nOpen formats accessible to any internal or external collaborator, citable DOIs. Acceptable? Possibly uncommon but does not offend. Might be 3. Could be 4 common strategies? Logging framework is common. Open sharing might be somewhat uncommon. I'd say 3.\n\